# tig dark colors — sourced by .tigrc through the theme-active.tigrc symlink,
# which toggle_theme.sh flips. Only what cannot be shared with the light theme
# belongs here; everything mode-agnostic stays in .tigrc.

# The cursor line. `blue` is the terminal's ANSI blue, and under the dark theme
# (Ghostty + Catppuccin Mocha) that is a pale #89b4fa: white text on it lands
# at 2.11:1 contrast, the brightest and least readable thing on screen. Borrow
# the editor's own selection colour the way the fzf dark theme does — `hi
# Search` in nvim/colors/vs_dark.vim is #264F78 — via color24 (#005f87), the
# nearest 256-colour index, as tigrc takes colour names and palette indexes but
# no hex. Ghostty themes remap only palette 0-15, so 24 keeps its xterm value.
# `default` fg is the terminal foreground, #D4D4D4: 4.74:1 on the bar, and the
# same fg/bg pairing fzf uses for fg+/bg+.
color cursor default color24 bold
